From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:58:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: enable the
 MAX77759's I2C bus

Enable USI13 as I2C at 400 kHz, as the Pixel 7 Pro does: the MAX77759
(Type-C port controller at 0x25, PMIC at 0x66, fuel gauge at 0x36,
charger at 0x69) sits there, on gpp25-0/1, in the Pixel 7's live device
tree too. Its devices stay undescribed for now: the Type-C port
controller would take over VBUS and the data role from the forced-VBUS
setup the USB PHY uses, and the USB link is the only way into the
phone.

With the bus up, user space can close the MAX77759's USB2 data switch
after a replug (TCPC vendor register 0x93), which the chip opens on
unplug; until a Type-C driver owns it, nothing else does, and the phone
stays off the bus.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B (7.3.0-rc6), with the touchscreen, GPU
and haptics: the bus probes as i2c-1, the TCPC's USBSW_CTRL reads 0x09
and the charger's CHG_DETAILS_00 0x60 (VBUS valid). After an unplug the
switch read 0x00; omamobile-usb-rescue set it back to 0x09 and USB
networking came back by itself, with no I2C errors.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts  | 21 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index 8763b7b5b..6fef68870 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
  *
  * USB (NCM + ACM), the cluster watchdogs from gs201.dtsi, a
  * simple-framebuffer on the buffer ABL leaves DPP0 scanning out, UFS, the
- * three keys, the touchscreen with its rails on the main PMIC, the GPU and
- * the haptics. The panel driver stays disabled.
+ * three keys, the touchscreen with its rails on the main PMIC, the GPU, the
+ * haptics and the MAX77759's I2C bus. The panel driver stays disabled.
  */
 
 /dts-v1/;
@@ -173,6 +173,23 @@ &ufs_0_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * MAX77759 (charger, Type-C port controller, fuel gauge) on USI13, as on
+ * the Pixel 7 Pro: TCPC 0x25, PMIC 0x66, fuel gauge 0x36, charger 0x69,
+ * bus pins gpp25-0/1. Its devices are not described yet: the Type-C port
+ * controller would take over VBUS and the data role from the forced-VBUS
+ * setup the USB PHY uses, and the USB link is our only way into the phone.
+ */
+&usi13 {
+	samsung,mode = <USI_MODE_I2C>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&hsi2c_13 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /*
  * Haptics: Cirrus Logic CS40L26A at 0x43 on PERIC0 USI8 (Google's I2C bus
  * 8), INTb on gpa8-1, RESET on gpp24-3, as on the Pixel 7 Pro. Boost and
